    "narrative": "The clear centerpiece for LawDog today is **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who carries an elite 80.53 score into his matchup against the southpaw Noah Schultz. While the opposing arm is capable, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** benefits from a strong lineup position and a favorable 18% skill adjustment based on recent plate discipline, making him our highest-ceiling asset. He is joined in the top tier by **Bryce Harper** (67.11) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (61.85). **Bryce Harper** remains a must-start despite the 33% rain risk at the venue, as his high xwOBA against right-handed pitching provides a reliable floor for RBI and R production. **Jung Hoo Lee** earns a strong recommendation due to a favorable matchup against Keider Montero, where a +10% platoon boost helps capitalize on his contact-heavy profile.\n\nSeveral marginal starts face tactical headwinds today, most notably **Cal Raleigh**, who is hampered by an unfavorable 3.19 xERA matchup against Drew Rasmussen, resulting in a thin 41.82 score. Our most difficult bench decision involved **Dylan Beavers** (48.11), who narrowly missed the cut. While **Dylan Beavers** offers a significant stolen base upside\u2014a priority category for our squad\u2014the optimizer favored the slightly higher projected output of **Gavin Sheets** and **Tyler Freeman**. Despite the lower floors, we are monitoring the 33% rain probability for **Luis Arraez**, **Justin Crawford**, and **Bryce Harper**; should the weather shift, we may look to swap in bench depth like **Lawrence Butler** or **Brendan Donovan** to ensure we maximize our daily efficiency and protect our game caps.",
